{"name":"Alter Ego","hex":"#69656d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alter ego","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An individual's alternate personality or persona; another self.","A very close and intimate friend."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alter_ego"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alter Ego (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Alter Ego is an American magazine devoted to comic books and comic-book creators of the 1930s to late-1960s periods comprising what fans and historians call the Golden Age and Silver Age of Comic Books."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Alter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alter_Ego_(magazine)","wikidata":"Q4736274"},{"title":"Alter Ego (Lisa album)","blocks":[{"text":"Alter Ego is the debut solo studio album by Thai rapper and singer Lisa. Released on February 28, 2025, by Lloud and RCA Records, the album marks Lisa's first solo release after departing from YG Entertainment and Interscope Records in 2023. She developed Alter Ego with a range of collaborators, including Ryan Tedder, Ilya Salmanzadeh, and Max Martin. It was conceived as a 15-track album exploring hip-hop, electropop and trap styles and features guest appearances from Rosalía and Tyla; Future, Megan Thee Stallion, Doja Cat and Raye also appear on digital editions. The album's subject matter explores Lisa's personality, fame, and success through the lens of various alter egos."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Lisa_-_Alter_Ego.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alter_Ego_(Lisa_album)","wikidata":"Q131288575"},{"title":"Alter ego","blocks":[{"text":"An alter ego means an alternate self, which is believed to be distinct from a person's normal or true original personality. Finding one's alter ego will require finding one's other self, one with a different personality. Additionally, the altered states of the ego may themselves be referred to as alterations."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alter_ego","wikidata":"Q201662"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/51/Alter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg/250px-Alter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Alter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/51/Alter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg/250px-Alter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlter-Ego-99-Jan2011.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/df/AlterEgo1.jpg/250px-AlterEgo1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/AlterEgo1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/df/AlterEgo1.jpg/250px-AlterEgo1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alter Ego #1 (1961). Cover art by Roy Thomas.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlterEgo1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0c/Lisa_-_Alter_Ego.png/250px-Lisa_-_Alter_Ego.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Lisa_-_Alter_Ego.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0c/Lisa_-_Alter_Ego.png/250px-Lisa_-_Alter_Ego.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALisa_-_Alter_Ego.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Jekyll-mansfield.jpg/330px-Jekyll-mansfield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Jekyll-mansfield.jpg/330px-Jekyll-mansfield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJekyll-mansfield.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Fred_Terry_in_The_Scarlet_Pimpernel_crop.jpg/250px-Fred_Terry_in_The_Scarlet_Pimpernel_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/Fred_Terry_in_The_Scarlet_Pimpernel_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Fred_Terry_in_The_Scarlet_Pimpernel_crop.jpg/250px-Fred_Terry_in_The_Scarlet_Pimpernel_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fred Terry as the Scarlet Pimpernel (alter ego of Sir Percy Blakeney) in the 1905 West End production of The Scarlet Pimpernel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFred_Terry_in_The_Scarlet_Pimpernel_crop.jpg"}],"sounds":{"alter ego":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/En-us-alter_ego.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/dd/En-us-alter_ego.ogg/En-us-alter_ego.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 4","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.